WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.826
Hi! Did you know that you, me, the flowers in the garden, and even this little bee are all made of tiny, tiny cells? Today let's find out about cells!

2
00:00:11.976 --> 00:00:18.114
A cell is the basic unit of a living thing, just like a brick is the basic unit of a house.

3
00:00:18.264 --> 00:00:25.122
Cells are too small to see with our eyes. We use a microscope to make them look many times bigger.

4
00:00:25.272 --> 00:00:33.714
Some living things have only one cell. Others, like people and big trees, have many, many cells.

5
00:00:33.864 --> 00:00:39.666
Let's look at a plant cell. It has several parts, and each part has its own job.

6
00:00:39.816 --> 00:00:47.874
The nucleus is the control centre of the cell. It controls all the activities in the cell, and it holds the genetic material.

7
00:00:48.024 --> 00:00:55.386
The cell membrane wraps around the cell. It controls which substances can go into the cell and which can come out.

8
00:00:55.536 --> 00:01:03.018
The cytoplasm is the jelly-like part inside the cell membrane. Most of the cell's activities take place here.

9
00:01:03.168 --> 00:01:10.218
A plant cell also has a firm cell wall on the outside. It protects the cell and gives it a fixed shape.

10
00:01:10.368 --> 00:01:17.466
These green parts are chloroplasts. They contain chlorophyll, which traps light so the plant can make food.

11
00:01:17.616 --> 00:01:25.242
This big part in the middle is the vacuole. It stores water and other substances.

12
00:01:25.392 --> 00:01:32.130
Now let's look at an animal cell. It also has a cell membrane, cytoplasm and a nucleus.

13
00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:37.098
But an animal cell has no cell wall, so it does not have a fixed shape.

14
00:01:37.248 --> 00:01:44.490
An animal cell has no chloroplasts either. That's why animals cannot make their own food, and need to eat.

15
00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:53.370
Both plant and animal cells have a cell membrane, cytoplasm and a nucleus. That is what they have in common.

16
00:01:53.520 --> 00:02:00.210
Watch out! Many pupils think all plant cells have chloroplasts. That is not true!

17
00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:09.666
Chloroplasts are only found in cells of the green parts of a plant, like the leaves. Roots grow underground, so root cells have no chloroplasts.

18
00:02:09.816 --> 00:02:17.442
So, to tell if a cell is a plant cell, look for the cell wall. Don't look only for chloroplasts.

19
00:02:17.592 --> 00:02:28.458
Your turn! A cell has a cell wall but no chloroplasts. What kind of cell could it be? Pause and think.

20
00:02:28.608 --> 00:02:36.450
It is a plant cell, such as a root cell, because only plant cells have a cell wall. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:47.250
Another one! Which part of a cell controls the movement of substances in and out of the cell? Pause and think.

22
00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:57.306
The answer is the cell membrane. The cell wall is on the outside, but it only protects and supports the cell. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:57.456 --> 00:03:07.290
Last one! Why can plants make their own food, while animals have to eat? Pause and think.

24
00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:18.450
Because cells in the green parts of a plant have chloroplasts, which trap light to make food. Animal cells have no chloroplasts. Did you get it right?

25
00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:32.394
Remember: all living things are made of cells. Cells have a cell membrane, cytoplasm and a nucleus. Plant cells also have a cell wall and a large vacuole, and cells in the green parts have chloroplasts.

26
00:03:32.544 --> 00:03:36.594
Now go and explore your garden!

